# Append-only journals: every parallel branch appends its own lines, so the
# default line-merge reports a conflict on every single concurrent branch.
# Union keeps both sides' lines instead of asking a human to pick one.
#
# Evidence for this rule, 2026-07-28: three of three branches merged that day
# (PRs #7, #8, #9) conflicted here and ONLY here. Not one code file conflicted.
#
# Caveat: union can leave a duplicate line if two branches append the same
# entry. That is visible in review and trivial to delete, which is a far
# cheaper failure than a hand-resolved conflict on every merge.
docs/journal/CHANGELOG.md  merge=union
docs/journal/DECISIONS.md     merge=union

# BUILD-STATE.md is deliberately NOT union. It is a mutable snapshot, not an
# append-only log, so unioning it would interleave two contradictory pictures
# of the same moment. It stays a manual resolve: rewrite it to the truth.

# LINE ENDINGS FOR THINGS LINUX EXECUTES, and this is not cosmetic.
# `docker-entrypoint.sh` runs as the container's ENTRYPOINT. Checked out on
# Windows with git's default conversion it gains CRLF, and the kernel then
# reads the shebang as `/bin/sh\r` and refuses to start the container with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". The image builds perfectly and dies on boot,
# on whichever machine git converted the file for (MB's commit adcc738).
*.sh text eol=lf
